course: dictionary
lesson: 14978
title: Fame and respect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Renown is a noun. It means fame, and the respect people give you for doing something well. A knight who wins many battles gains renown, so people all over the land know his name and admire him.
explain: Renown is not just being known. «The scientist won world renown for her cure for the illness.» The clues are «world» and «won», so renown means many people, even far away, admire her for real achievement.
explain: Look out for the adjective «renowned». «The town is renowned for its cheese» means the town is famous for its cheese. Renown is uncountable, so we say «great renown», never «a renown» or «renowns».
fact: Renown is a noun meaning fame and respect for doing something well.
fact: Renown is uncountable, so write «great renown», not «a renown».
fact: Useful phrases are «of renown», «win renown» and «world renown».
fact: «Renowned» is the adjective: «renowned for its cheese» means famous for its cheese.
exercise: «The knight fought bravely and won great renown across the land.» What does renown mean here? | Fear of the dark | A tired horse | *Fame and respect for doing something well | A long, heavy sword
exercise: Which word is the adjective made from renown? | Renownful | Renownly | Renowning | *Renowned
exercise: Which sentence uses renown correctly? | The scientist had renowns across the world. | The scientist had a renown across the world. | *The scientist had great renown across the world. | The scientist had renown-ed across the world.
test: «The painter won renown for her paintings of the sea.» What does renown mean? | *Fame and respect for doing something well | Money earned from selling paintings | A small boat on the sea | Paint on the walls of a house
test: Which sentence uses the adjective correctly? | The town is renowning for its cheese. | The town is renowns for its cheese. | The town is renown for its cheese. | *The town is renowned for its cheese.
exam: Which best defines renown? | A loud, sudden noise | *Fame and respect for doing something well | Lost, forgotten and unknown | Money earned from work
